// Type checking for frontend/e2e.
//
// "root" here means the e2e tree that sits at the frontend root, not the
// repository's root-level config files, which deliberately stay out; see the
// boundary note below.
//
// The second half of the same hole tsconfig.e2e.json closed. That one covers
// tests/e2e, 38 files. This covers e2e, 86 - the older of the two Playwright
// trees (first commit 2026-03-26 against 2026-05-12) and not a dead one: both
// were edited on 2026-08-29. Six of the sixteen playwright*.config.ts files
// point testDir into this tree, and two more at e2e-match and playwright, which
// stay outside every project: eight of our sixteen e2e configurations were
// driving code that nothing type checked, and this closes six of the eight. We
// only found that out because a spec had to be checked through a scratchpad
// config, there being nothing in the repository able to check it.
//
// A third project rather than another entry in tsconfig.e2e.json's include,
// and definitely not in the base include, for the reason recorded in
// tsconfig.e2e.json and ci.yml: the whole-program check over src already OOM'd
// at a 6 GB heap, runs at 9 GB now, and macOS skips it outright because 9 GB
// exceeds that runner's RAM. Nothing here imports from src (measured: zero
// files in either e2e tree import `@/` or reach into ../src), so this program
// stays at its own 86 files and costs seconds. Separate from tests/e2e as well
// so that each tree can be checked on its own, and so a failure names which
// half it came from.
//
// It extends the base config and overrides no compiler option, on purpose.
// Exempting this directory from strictness would leave the same hole under a
// nicer name.
//
// The boundary, written down because the count is easy to misread: this covers
// e2e only. After it lands, 25 tracked .ts/.tsx files are still outside every
// project - 17 root-level config and setup files, e2e-match (2), playwright
// (2), tests/pwa (2), tests/splash (1) and scripts (1). Closing 86 of 111 is
// not closing 111.
//
// The exclude is not a strictness exemption, it is what keeps this gate reading
// the repository rather than the disk. Both patterns are copied from .gitignore
// lines 70 and 71: throwaway debug and diagnostic specs live in this directory
// untracked, and 18 of them were sitting here when this was written. Without the
// exclude, tsc reads them - the first run over this tree reported 43 errors, of
// which 3 came from files no checkout will ever contain, so the same command
// would have answered differently here and in CI, and a developer mid-debug
// would meet a red gate over a file they were about to delete. If a new ignore
// rule for this directory is added to .gitignore, it belongs here too; these two
// lists are kept in step by hand and nothing checks that they are.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "include": ["e2e"],
  "exclude": ["e2e/_*.spec.ts", "e2e/*-diagnostic.spec.ts"]
}
